1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,643
Robinhood Chain put US stocks on-chain.

2
00:00:02,843 --> 00:00:06,457
Strike turns them into weekly options vaults, paid in USDG.

3
00:00:06,907 --> 00:00:08,993
Holding a stock token earns nothing extra.

4
00:00:09,193 --> 00:00:14,747
Options on the chain are new, and none lets an AI agent make the weekly call inside rules the contract enforces.

5
00:00:15,197 --> 00:00:20,752
Stock tokens also have traps: a multiplier applied twice, prices frozen over the weekend, two layers of pause.

6
00:00:20,952 --> 00:00:25,833
SafeStockFeed handles each one, and our monitor checks eight mainnet stock tokens, live.

7
00:00:26,283 --> 00:00:30,514
Stylus makes solving the strike on-chain 3.3 times cheaper per proposal.

8
00:00:30,964 --> 00:00:34,320
An AI agent picks each week's strike, but never touches the funds.

9
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:39,391
The mandate is fixed on-chain: a delta band, a premium floor, a maximum size.

10
00:00:39,591 --> 00:00:42,467
Break it, and the agent's bond is slashed to depositors.

11
00:00:42,667 --> 00:00:47,644
Agent one is ERC-8004 identity 114, with a public reputation.

12
00:00:48,094 --> 00:00:52,997
Deposit TSLA, and each week the vault sells a covered call, for a premium in USDG.

13
00:00:53,197 --> 00:00:57,075
Deposit USDG, and the put vault pays you to wait for a lower price.

14
00:00:57,525 --> 00:01:01,287
It is live at strike-options.vercel.app.

15
00:01:01,737 --> 00:01:08,389
Test it without a wallet: the playground runs any proposal against a live mandate, and the proof page links every claim to its evidence.

16
00:01:08,839 --> 00:01:16,173
On testnet, a buyer agent paid 10.01 USDG of premium, and a reckless agent's 10 USDG slash was paid to depositors.

17
00:01:16,623 --> 00:01:24,225
Cboe's BXM index has covered-call data back to 1986, and our backtest shows 25 to 46% lower volatility than holding.

18
00:01:24,675 --> 00:01:27,252
Stonkhouse and Archer Markets let traders pick strikes.

19
00:01:27,452 --> 00:01:30,627
In Strike, a bonded agent proposes, and the contract checks.

20
00:01:31,077 --> 00:01:34,955
Strike takes ten percent of positive weekly net premium, half to the agent.

21
00:01:35,155 --> 00:01:36,517
A losing week pays nothing.

22
00:01:36,967 --> 00:01:45,155
Behind it are 802 tests and proofs: 432 Foundry tests, 9 properties proven with Halmos, and 99.1% line coverage.

23
00:01:45,355 --> 00:01:49,329
An internal review found 11 issues, one of them High, and all are fixed.

24
00:01:49,779 --> 00:01:53,018
Next come a capped mainnet vault, more tickers and put spreads.

25
00:01:53,468 --> 00:01:58,072
Strike: weekly options vaults on Robinhood Chain, with agents the contract holds to their mandate.

